517
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:22,077
Yeah, but if I drink this stuff?

518
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:26,500
I'll be the big captain guy of
some grand fleet, is that right?

519
00:31:27,500 --> 00:31:28,330
Uh, yeah.

520
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:34,360
With 5 ,600 followers, you'd be one of
the most impressive pirates on the seas.

521
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:40,177
I mean, you're gonna be king of the
pirates eventually, no doubt about it.

522
00:31:40,260 --> 00:31:44,789
But it's a big world, so if you want to
conquer it, then you gotta think big.

523
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:47,200
He doesn't care. Give it up.

524
00:31:47,860 --> 00:31:50,480
You're wasting your time. Huh?

525
00:31:51,180 --> 00:31:53,940
So, put this in a beer mug.

526
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:55,460
I'll drink it.

527
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:58,720
I said it's not for taste, it's for a vow!

528
00:31:59,340 --> 00:32:00,700
Why, Straw Hat?

529
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:03,901
A massive military force
could be at your command.

530
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:07,280
The men who stand before
you are almighty warriors,

531
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:10,517
and yet we would have been
undone without your help.

532
00:32:10,600 --> 00:32:13,600
Someday you'll find yourself
in the same situation.

533
00:32:13,820 --> 00:32:15,080
Not my style!

534
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:17,190
Huh?

535
00:32:17,273 --> 00:32:18,103
What's with that look?

536
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:24,517
Anyway, are people getting ready
for a party, cause I smell food.

537
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:25,430
That's great.

538
00:32:25,540 --> 00:32:26,817
Just change the subject.

539
00:32:26,900 --> 00:32:28,677
You're pissing me off, Straw Hat.

540
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:29,590
Listen,

541
00:32:29,673 --> 00:32:33,297
you should be grateful that a star like
me is willing to fly under your flag.

542
00:32:33,380 --> 00:32:34,897
Let's force him to drink it.

543
00:32:34,980 --> 00:32:38,760
I know you saved us, but we're
strong enough to kick your ass.

544
00:32:38,960 --> 00:32:40,489
I thought he was the boss.

545
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:41,700
Don't be so rude.

546
00:32:42,420 --> 00:32:43,420
Here's the thing.

547
00:32:43,600 --> 00:32:45,920
I want to be the king of the pirates.

548
00:32:46,220 --> 00:32:48,161
I don't need to be some big shot.

549
00:32:51,380 --> 00:32:52,210
Huh?

550
00:32:52,293 --> 00:32:53,640
Even for him, that's dumb.

551
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:58,120
Damn, that's good stuff. Knew it.

552
00:32:58,320 --> 00:32:59,200
You's a cop!

553
00:32:59,460 --> 00:33:00,540
That's so gross!

554
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:02,220
Ooh, me next.

555
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:03,460
I want some too.

556
00:33:06,180 --> 00:33:07,320
How about this?

557
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:10,580
If I'm ever in trouble,
I'll call you guys for help.

558
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:14,897
And I know you'll save me, because that's
what friends do for each other, right?

559
00:33:14,980 --> 00:33:18,037
I don't have to be a big shot
or have a whole fleet for that.

560
00:33:18,120 --> 00:33:21,060
And if you're ever in trouble call us.

561
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:23,160
I'm happy to help anytime

562
00:33:23,760 --> 00:33:26,348
I couldn't have beat
Mingo without you guys.

563
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:27,951
So we're friends for life

564
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:32,200
You know.

565
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:35,860
It took a second, but I get it now.

566
00:33:37,020 --> 00:33:41,314
And I think I understand what it means
for you to be king of the pirates.

567
00:33:42,260 --> 00:33:46,080
It's not about being big, but being free.

568
00:33:48,260 --> 00:33:49,440
What was that?

569
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:51,860
Cannon fire!

570
00:33:52,080 --> 00:33:54,020
Is it the Navy? Can't be.

571
00:33:54,300 --> 00:33:55,359
They're all stuck.

572
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:57,912
I sewed their ships together extra tight.

573
00:33:59,340 --> 00:34:00,170
Fire!

574
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:03,499
Columbus can take care of this one.

575
00:34:03,620 --> 00:34:06,260
Sorry, but we're still busy here.

576
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:09,000
Whoever it is, take them out. Sir!

577
00:34:09,460 --> 00:34:11,860
I know you have Straw Hats on your ship.

578
00:34:12,180 --> 00:34:14,340
Hand them over or pay the price.

579
00:34:14,580 --> 00:34:17,080
You don't want to defy us.

580
00:34:19,100 --> 00:34:21,680
Get back on land! It's dangerous!

581
00:34:22,340 --> 00:34:25,080
But if we leave, Fujitora
might attack Lucy!

582
00:34:25,580 --> 00:34:26,780
Return fire!

583
00:34:31,020 --> 00:34:31,940
Fire!

584
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,520
Let him sink!

585
00:34:46,020 --> 00:34:48,817
Look, the rubble's raining
down on the enemy's ship!

586
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:49,760
Well, not us!

587
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:16,860
This is my parting gift, Straw Hat.

588
00:35:23,640 --> 00:35:24,560
Freedom.

589
00:35:25,140 --> 00:35:25,970
Right.

590
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:28,177
That song Mr.

591
00:35:28,260 --> 00:35:30,380
Luffy wants, it's beautiful.

592
00:35:31,060 --> 00:35:32,657
He's the greatest.

593
00:35:32,740 --> 00:35:33,780
They love him!

594
00:35:33,940 --> 00:35:34,880
Even more!

595
00:35:40,540 --> 00:35:41,620
You know what?

596
00:35:42,100 --> 00:35:44,620
Let's do the oath, because we want to.

597
00:35:45,100 --> 00:35:48,218
It doesn't matter if Straw
Heart won't drink with us.

598
00:35:49,520 --> 00:35:50,880
He makes a good point.

599
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:55,900
If you can do what you want, so can we.

600
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:58,360
You wanna talk about freedom?

601
00:35:58,540 --> 00:35:59,775
Well, we have it too!

602
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:01,820
I didn't think of that!

603
00:36:16,940 --> 00:36:17,770
Mr.

604
00:36:17,853 --> 00:36:24,480
Luffy, I'll raise this sake cup and offer
up an oath, the long-witted. Huh? An oath?

605
00:36:24,980 --> 00:36:26,780
All right, here goes.

606
00:36:28,580 --> 00:36:32,640
We'll become the proud
followers of Straw Hat Luffy.

607
00:36:33,320 --> 00:36:38,040
Therefore, in rain or in shine, we
shall serve as his sword and his shield.

608
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:43,900
To repay our debt to him, the seven of
us offer a loyalty of our own accord.

609
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:48,980
As we drink these cups, let us pledge
both our lives and our hearts alike.

610
00:37:13,340 --> 00:37:15,780
I didn't say you guys could do that!

611
00:37:16,560 --> 00:37:18,442
Yeah, I guess it's official now!

612
00:37:18,580 --> 00:37:20,880
Let's get this party started already!

613
00:37:22,360 --> 00:37:24,660
I thought you'd never ask!

614
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:27,520
Let us feast in honor
of the Straw Hat fleet!

615
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:30,860
5 ,600 strong! Yeah!

616
00:37:32,700 --> 00:37:33,780
How underhanded.

617
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:37,147
They just do what they want.

618
00:37:37,340 --> 00:37:38,500
I like their style.

619
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:40,480
Looking good, Big Boss.

620
00:37:40,740 --> 00:37:43,160
Can't wait to work with you. What?

621
00:37:44,580 --> 00:37:47,020
Hey, I did not drink this stuff.

622
00:37:47,840 --> 00:37:50,680
I know the cup's empty,
but that's not on me.

623
00:37:51,640 --> 00:37:53,400
Yeah, we don't care.

624
00:37:54,100 --> 00:37:56,457
I won't bother trying to force your hand,

625
00:37:56,540 --> 00:38:00,599
but we can still swear our loyalty
to you whether you like it or not.

626
00:38:00,860 --> 00:38:03,857
That means, when you're in
trouble, we'll come running.

627
00:38:03,940 --> 00:38:07,097
If you have friends who are willing
to do that for nothing in return,

628
00:38:07,180 --> 00:38:08,533
you should be grateful.

629
00:38:08,820 --> 00:38:13,360
All we ask is that you engrave
our names and faces on your heart.

630
00:38:13,560 --> 00:38:14,400
Hey, honey.

631
00:38:16,180 --> 00:38:17,010
He's gone.

632
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:19,280
Look at the main course!

633
00:38:19,520 --> 00:38:21,037
It's a fighting fish steak!

634
00:38:21,120 --> 00:38:22,197
Give me some of that!

635
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:23,456
Don't climb on poop!

636
00:38:23,640 --> 00:38:24,700
That's unhygienic!

637
00:38:24,900 --> 00:38:26,665
Would you stop crying already?

638
00:38:27,100 --> 00:38:30,260
I was so touched by his
words, I may never stop!

639
00:38:30,860 --> 00:38:32,680
Just leave me to my tears.

640
00:38:33,020 --> 00:38:35,617
Leo, I think we're all
about to leave the port.

641
00:38:35,700 --> 00:38:36,994
Will you stay and eat?

642
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:39,736
There's no way we'd miss the banquet.

643
00:38:40,080 --> 00:38:42,577
We can take the yellow
cubs back to Dressrosa.

644
00:38:42,660 --> 00:38:44,120
Don't worry about it.

645
00:38:45,080 --> 00:38:46,540
Are we setting sail now?

646
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:49,280
Right, the bosses, time to go.

647
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:50,580
Hoist the sail.

648
00:39:08,180 --> 00:39:10,500
I see the rubble raining down.

649
00:39:10,700 --> 00:39:13,097
Did it wipe out Straw Hat and his friends?

650
00:39:13,180 --> 00:39:15,121
No, it's missing all the targets.

651
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:17,020
You've got to be kidding me.

652
00:39:26,900 --> 00:39:31,240
That day, Dressrosa experienced some
very unusual weather conditions.

653
00:39:31,600 --> 00:39:36,365
But in the end, their heavy downpour of
rubble gradually gave way to sunny skies.

654
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:44,560
Truth be told, I had no right to
chase you down in the first place.

655
00:39:46,680 --> 00:39:47,510
Also,

656
00:39:47,700 --> 00:39:52,017
though I probably shouldn't say
this out loud You really did clean

657
00:39:52,100 --> 00:39:56,080
up the government's mess here in
Dressrosa And for your courage,

658
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:58,440
you have my eternal gratitude

659
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:04,200
I heard that

660
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:12,200
All right, guys, let's raise our cuffs

661
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:17,400
Our team kicked the Mingo family's ass!

662
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:20,897
So here's to us! And...

663
00:40:20,980 --> 00:40:22,020
to victory!

664
00:40:23,340 --> 00:40:24,170
Yeah!

665
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:30,190
Let's party!

666
00:40:31,820 --> 00:40:33,160
You guys were awesome!

667
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:35,480
Thanks, Froland!

668
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:39,180
Sorry, Lind, you're the best! Duh!

669
00:40:42,320 --> 00:40:43,150
Rooster!

670
00:40:44,560 --> 00:40:46,060
Mr. Luffy!

671
00:40:50,140 --> 00:40:51,100
Honey!

672
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:54,390
Make a toast!

673
00:40:55,180 --> 00:40:56,640
Chew us!

674
00:41:09,560 --> 00:41:11,560
Seems like they made it after all.

675
00:41:12,820 --> 00:41:14,600
I was worried for a sec.

676
00:41:15,860 --> 00:41:17,920
I hope they'll come visit.

677
00:41:26,200 --> 00:41:27,840
Is it warm?

678
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:33,790
Yes.

679
00:41:34,900 --> 00:41:37,180
It's much better this way.

680
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:46,720
Oh, are you crying, Dad? What?

681
00:41:47,100 --> 00:41:49,020
No, I never cry.

682
00:41:49,280 --> 00:41:50,221
Don't be absurd.

683
00:41:55,740 --> 00:41:56,570
Wait!

684
00:42:11,180 --> 00:42:13,380
Hey, get over here.

685
00:42:14,460 --> 00:42:15,400
Ow!

686
00:42:17,100 --> 00:42:18,600
Another round?

687
00:42:19,240 --> 00:42:20,860
Yeah, any time.

688
00:42:21,460 --> 00:42:22,290
Let go!

689
00:42:22,780 --> 00:42:25,300
Press nose for advanced hair features.

690
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:41,860
I know you've got places to go, but
we'll see you again, right? Of course.

691
00:42:42,120 --> 00:42:43,040
We'll be back.

692
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:44,940
I can't wait!

693
00:42:45,380 --> 00:42:46,520
Great news!

694
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:47,980
Well, hello.

695
00:42:51,340 --> 00:42:53,900
After the hard-fought battle in Dressrosa,

696
00:42:54,080 --> 00:42:57,300
a very unconventional vow
was made over cups of sake.

697
00:42:59,800 --> 00:43:00,880
By coincidence,

698
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:02,437
or by the hand of fate,

699
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:07,461
when the pass of seven mighty warriors
crossed, they pledged their loyalty to Luffy.

700
00:43:08,340 --> 00:43:11,457
Their own adventures will
bring them strength and renown,

701
00:43:11,540 --> 00:43:12,917
and one day in the future,

702
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:17,000
they will play a part in a great
incident of historic proportions.

703
00:43:18,660 --> 00:43:23,000
But for now, at least, that's a
story no one could have anticipated.
